%N A400522 The exponent of the highest power of 2 dividing the n-th number whose number of divisors is a power of 2 (A036537).
%H A400522 Amiram Eldar, <a href="/A400522/b400522.txt">Table of n, a(n) for n = 1..10000</a>
%F A400522 a(n) = A007814(A036537(n)).
%F A400522 a(n) <= A372466(n).
%F A400522 Asymptotic mean: Limit_{m->oo} (1/m) * Sum_{k=1..m} a(k) = Sum_{k>=1} (2^k-1)/2^(2^k-1) / Sum_{k>=0} 1/2^(2^k-1) = 0.56964770515522524972... .
%t A400522 pow2Q[n_] := n == 2^IntegerExponent[n, 2]; IntegerExponent[Select[Range[150], pow2Q[DivisorSigma[0, #]] &], 2]
%o A400522 (PARI) ispowtwo(n) = n >> valuation(n, 2) == 1;
%o A400522 list(kmax) = for(k = 1, kmax, if(ispowtwo(numdiv(k)), print1(valuation(k, 2), ", ")));
%Y A400522 Cf. A007814, A036537, A372466.
%Y A400522 Similar sequences: 1-A373550 (squarefree), A383004 (cubefree), A383005 (biquadratefree), A383006 (powerful), A383007 (cubefull), A383029 (exponentially odd), A386536 (cubefree but not squarefree).
%K A400522 nonn,easy,new
